    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Description\n\nI recently migrated to mini.surround from nvim-surround. First of all, good job with the plugin, the dot-repeat works great!\r\n\r\nThe only thing I'm currently missing, is an insert mode mapping for surrounding things. nvim-surround had `<C-g>s` for inline-surround and `<C-g>S` for line-surround. Could this functionality please be added to mini.surround?",
    "closed_at": "2024-07-26T07:22:45Z",
