    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\r\n\r\nI hoped that something making a mapping to `<C-o>sa` would work, but it does not due to complications of how mapping are implemented.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, properly adding Insert mode mappings would require a lot of user configuration to be useful (like keys for Insert mode mapping for every action). Reading more about what [`<C-g>s`](https://github.com/kylechui/nvim-surround/blob/ec2dc7671067e0086cdf29c2f5df2dd909d5f71f/doc/nvim-surround.txt#L60) and [`<C-g>S`](https://github.com/kylechui/nvim-surround/blob/ec2dc7671067e0086cdf29c2f5df2dd909d5f71f/doc/nvim-surround.txt#L106) do in 'kylechui/nvim-surround', they can be replicated with the following user mappings (because thankfully surrounding visual selection after `<C-o>` works):\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<C-g>s', '<C-o>vsa', { remap = true })\r\nvim.keymap.set('i', '<C-g>S', '<C-o>Vsa', { remap = true })\r\n```\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
            "created_at": "2024-07-26T07:22:45Z",
